title: SecondLoopWisteria2
tags:
---

???: BZZTTTTTT…
As you head towards the hall outside, you are stopped by a strange vibration coming from your pockets.
Immediately afterwards, a hellish cacophony of loud, abrasive static erupts from it.
You cover your ears instinctively. The constant barrage of screeching, violent noise makes it hard to think.
You put one hand in your pocket and take out the culprit: Your radio.
You bought this while outside of Solster, and brought it here to keep informed with the outside world still. It has never done anything like this before.
You take the radio closer to you, against your ears’ pleads.
-> Hello?
    No response. Not at first.
	As you fiddle with the dial and try to tune the radio, you can barely hear a voice coming through amongst all the static.
	???: ….H..P…HEL..ME….
	The voice sounds in distress. The abrasive static heightens it, making it sounds almost like someone being tortured.
	Something feels very wrong about this. This isn’t regular radio static from being attuned to the wrong channel. It is as if something is directly interfering with the radio.
        << if $TechMajor == true >>
	        The radio itself shows no signs of wear, tear, or malfunction. The problem is completely external.
        << endif >>
    Wisteria: What in the mother is that screaming noise?
	You turn towards Wisteria. She is covering her ears and closing her eyes as you turn to her.
        << if $PsychMajor == true >>
	        She is sensitive to loud sounds. Maybe she should get tested for Adult Autism herself.
        << elseif $TechMajor == true >>
	        She seems to be sensitive to loud sounds. An exploitable weakness, if you really wanted to cause her discomfort.
        << endif >>
-> (Turn back to Wisteria) Can you hear this too?
    Wisteria is covering her ears and closing her eyes as you turn to her.
    << if $PsychMajor == true >>
	    She is sensitive to loud sounds. Maybe she should get tested for Adult Autism herself.
    << elseif $TechMajor == true >>
	    She seems to be sensitive to loud sounds. An exploitable weakness, if you really wanted to cause her discomfort.
    << endif >>
	Wisteria: What in the mother is that screaming noise?
	You take that as a yes. It is reassuring at least to know for sure this isn’t a hallucination this time.
	She is right, though. There is a voice screaming in the static, though hard to make out.
	???: ….H..P…HEL..ME….
	The voice sounds in distress. The abrasive static heightens it, making it sounds almost like someone being tortured.
	Something feels very wrong about this. This isn’t regular radio static from being attuned to the wrong channel. It is as if something is directly interfering with the radio.
    << if $TechMajor == true >>
	    The radio itself shows no signs of wear, tear, or malfunction. The problem is completely external.
    << endif >>

        -> My radio is making some crazy static noises on its own.
            Wisteria: Yeah, I can hear that, you moron. Take that thing out of my office!
	        Wisteria: Just go to Nauka Square or something, I’m sure they can figure out what’s wrong with it there.
        -> Do you know what might be up with my radio?
            Wisteria: Do I look like a mechanic to you? Drag me down if I know.
	        Wisteria: Go to Nauka Square. I’m sure they’ll know what to do with it.
	        Wisteria: Now take that screeching thing out of my office!
Nauka Square. You remember Fabian mentioned it briefly, back in… Well in your “first” first day back in Solster.
You had never heard of it in your youth. Is it a new place? Or was it just not that relevant to you back then?
Fabian mentioned that there was a scientist there. Maybe going to Nauka Square could help you with figuring out what in the world happened with your ‘time travel’.
You don’t have much better leads right now, unless you want to hunt down who “Deniz” is. Nauka Square it is.

